00:00:23.281 --> 00:00:30.535
What you get: the architecture of a global, multi-seller marketplace in the style Amazon has described publicly.

10
00:00:30.815 --> 00:00:44.895
It covers: an always-writable cart;. one catalog entry per product, with many sellers' offers and a buy box winner;. a delivery promise computed from fulfilment-centre stock;. a page composed from many services;.

11
00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:50.959
order pipelines as workflows;. cells and shuffle sharding to contain failures.

12
00:00:51.239 --> 00:00:52.498
What the labs measured:

13
00:00:52.778 --> 00:01:01.247
L1 (cart merge): in 20,000 fully partitioned cart sessions, last-writer-wins lost 36,206 adds.

14
00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:09.826
Dynamo-style union kept adds (6 lost to clock skew) but resurrected 12,184 removed items.

15
00:01:10.106 --> 00:01:13.093
An OR-Set cart got 100% of carts right.

16
00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:16.189
L2 (buy box, real PostgreSQL):

17
00:01:17.539 --> 00:01:22.104
Reading a maintained buy-box row is faster than computing the winner per page:

18
00:01:22.384 --> 00:01:31.088
57k versus 29k reads per second, p99 0.29 versus 0.49 ms.

19
00:01:31.368 --> 00:01:35.208
Maintaining it cuts repricing throughput by ~30%.

20
00:01:35.488 --> 00:01:40.352
A forced interleaving shows the race: two concurrent reprices leave the wrong winner.

21
00:01:40.632 --> 00:01:42.381
A per-product lock fixes it.

22
00:01:42.661 --> 00:01:56.741
L3 (delivery promise): an exhaustive planner cuts cost per order by 17% (110.9 rupees, then 91.9 rupees) and split orders from 54% to 36%.

23
00:01:57.021 --> 00:02:03.165
The share delivered within the promise is identical, 63.5%, for all strategies.

24
00:02:03.445 --> 00:02:09.440
Only stocking the top 300 SKUs everywhere moves it, to 68.7%.

25
00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:18.193
L4 (shuffle sharding): with one poison customer, fixed shards take out 25% of other customers completely.

26
00:02:18.473 --> 00:02:27.219
Shuffle shards of 2 of 8 workers take out 3.6%, and 5 of 80 take out 0%, matching 1 or C(n,k).

27
00:02:27.499 --> 00:02:28.481
