00:06:15.553 --> 00:06:16.427
Part 2.

93
00:06:16.707 --> 00:06:18.606
Core Concepts, Beginner to Deep.

94
00:06:19.856 --> 00:06:21.883
Intuition: a mall, not a shop.

95
00:06:22.163 --> 00:06:24.189
A single retailer owns its shelves.

96
00:06:24.469 --> 00:06:32.448
A marketplace is a mall: thousands of shops (sellers) sell the same product, and the mall decides which shop's offer to show first.

97
00:06:32.728 --> 00:06:38.083
It runs the checkout counters, the warehouses (for sellers who use them), and the delivery vans.

98
00:06:38.363 --> 00:06:47.771
The platform's job is to make the mall feel like one shop to the customer, while treating every seller fairly and keeping the mall open whatever happens in one aisle.

99
00:06:49.121 --> 00:06:50.081
Requirements.

100
00:06:50.361 --> 00:06:51.726
Here is a quick table:

101
00:06:52.006 --> 00:06:53.307
Type, and Requirement.

102
00:06:53.587 --> 00:06:54.462
Functional:

103
00:06:54.742 --> 00:07:09.910
Browse and search a catalog; product pages with offers; cart; checkout; payment; delivery promise and tracking; returns; seller listing, pricing and inventory; reviews; recommendations; membership (for example, free shipping).

104
00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:12.601
Scale (assumptions, B1 estimation):

105
00:07:12.881 --> 00:07:23.782
300M products and 2B offers; 50M daily active shoppers; 10 times traffic on sale days; 5M orders per day normal and 30M on peak days.

106
00:07:24.062 --> 00:07:24.979
Latency:

107
00:07:25.259 --> 00:07:29.398
Product page p99 at most 300 ms at the edge.

108
00:07:29.678 --> 00:07:33.049
Add-to-cart p99 at most 100 ms.

109
00:07:33.329 --> 00:07:36.251
