343
00:22:02.214 --> 00:22:03.857
Design Document Excerpt.

344
00:22:05.107 --> 00:22:05.853
Note:

345
00:22:06.133 --> 00:22:09.099
Design Document (excerpt), Buy Box Service.

346
00:22:09.379 --> 00:22:15.651
Context, Product pages compute the winning offer per request from the offers table (L2 path A).

347
00:22:15.931 --> 00:22:22.971
Page p99 budget pressure, and repricers generate ~5k offer changes per second at peak.

348
00:22:23.251 --> 00:22:31.827
Decision, Maintain a buybox row per product, updated in the same transaction as each offer change, under a per-product advisory lock.

349
00:22:32.107 --> 00:22:33.429
Pages read the row.

350
00:22:33.709 --> 00:22:35.523
Checkout re-validates the offer.

351
00:22:35.803 --> 00:22:48.624
Related ADRs, ADR-I01 to 1 cart OR-Set; ADR-I01 to 2 promise re-validation at checkout; ADR-I01 to 3 shuffle-sharded front ends.

352
00:22:48.904 --> 00:22:49.864
Requirements.

353
00:22:51.214 --> 00:22:52.046
R1:

354
00:22:52.326 --> 00:22:57.105
Product page buy-box read p99 at most 1 ms at the service.

355
00:22:57.385 --> 00:22:58.217
R2:

356
00:22:58.497 --> 00:23:02.699
After any committed offer change, the buy box is correct for that product.

357
00:23:02.979 --> 00:23:04.451
No lasting wrong winner.

358
00:23:04.731 --> 00:23:05.585
R3:

359
00:23:05.865 --> 00:23:08.787
Sustain 5k offer changes per second at peak.

360
00:23:09.067 --> 00:23:09.963
R4:

361
00:23:10.243 --> 00:23:14.531
Checkout never charges a price different from the one validated at checkout.

362
00:23:14.811 --> 00:23:15.686
R5:

363
00:23:15.966 --> 00:23:19.315
A full rebuild is possible in 10 min, as a repair tool.

364
00:23:19.595 --> 00:23:21.003
Decisions in detail.

365
00:23:22.353 --> 00:23:23.484
Maintained winner.

366
00:23:23.764 --> 00:23:32.980
L2 shows read p99 0.29 ms versus 0.49 ms, and about 2 times the read throughput.

367
00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:34.881
Per-product serialization.

368
00:23:35.161 --> 00:23:38.191
L2's forced interleaving shows the race without it.

369
00:23:38.471 --> 00:23:42.161
The lock cost ~14% of throughput in the price war.

370
00:23:42.441 --> 00:23:48.671
A nightly consistency check compares against a from-scratch computation and alerts on any mismatch.

371
00:23:48.951 --> 00:23:53.879
Checkout re-validation against the offer row covers any page-to-checkout staleness.

372
00:23:55.229 --> 00:23:56.253
Consequences.

373
00:23:56.533 --> 00:24:00.031
Offer writes are ~30% more expensive (L2).

374
00:24:00.311 --> 00:24:05.026
One hot product's repricing serializes (acceptable: it's one product).

375
00:24:05.306 --> 00:24:07.375
A rebuild job exists for repair.

