383
00:24:29.621 --> 00:24:31.861
L1, The always-writable cart.

384
00:24:32.141 --> 00:24:33.080
Requirement:

385
00:24:33.360 --> 00:24:39.653
Add-to-cart never fails, and after the partition heals the cart holds exactly what the shopper intended.

386
00:24:39.933 --> 00:24:42.707
This lab simulates 20,000 shopper sessions.

387
00:24:42.987 --> 00:24:51.413
Every request goes to a random one of 3 partitioned replicas, and clocks are skewed by up to ±150 ms.

388
00:24:52.763 --> 00:24:55.921
Here is the Java code, CartMergeL1.java.

389
00:24:56.201 --> 00:25:00.233
It runs to 102 lines; the full listing is in the chapter.

390
00:25:00.513 --> 00:25:03.713
L1, The always-writable cart (Dynamo-style).

391
00:25:03.993 --> 00:25:09.539
Three replicas accept cart writes during a partition; afterwards the. versions are merged.

392
00:25:09.819 --> 00:25:20.550
Compare: last-writer-wins (LWW), Dynamo's union of siblings (adds survive, deletes can. resurrect), and an OR-Set cart (adds and removes both survive).

393
00:25:20.830 --> 00:25:23.561
Counts lost adds and resurrected removes.

394
00:25:26.411 --> 00:25:27.328
On screen:

395
00:25:27.608 --> 00:25:46.445
20,000 partitioned cart sessions, 95,886 adds and 27,318 removes spread over 3. replicas (clock skew ±150 ms). merge strategy lost adds resurrected removes cart exactly right.

396
00:25:46.725 --> 00:25:55.835
LWW (whole cart, newest timestamp) 36,206 2,604 8.3%.

397
00:25:56.115 --> 00:26:02.152
Dynamo union of siblings 6 12,184 52.3%.

398
00:26:02.432 --> 00:26:07.488
OR-Set (add-tags, remove-tags) 0 0 100.0%.

399
00:26:10.338 --> 00:26:11.191
Reading it:

400
00:26:11.471 --> 00:26:15.461
Last-writer-wins keeps one replica's cart and throws away the rest.

401
00:26:15.741 --> 00:26:21.373
It lost 36,206 adds, and only 8% of carts ended up right.

402
00:26:21.653 --> 00:26:28.181
Union of siblings keeps nearly every add, but brings back 12,184 removed items.

403
00:26:28.461 --> 00:26:33.218
This is the deleted items can resurface behaviour the Dynamo paper accepts.

404
00:26:33.498 --> 00:26:39.322
The 6 lost adds come from clock skew reordering a remove and a re-add on the same replica.

405
00:26:39.602 --> 00:26:41.458
The OR-Set gets every cart right.

406
00:26:41.738 --> 00:26:46.495
Each add carries a tag, and a remove deletes only the tags the client had seen.

407
00:26:47.845 --> 00:26:52.155
The scenario is the worst case: the whole session happens during a partition.

408
00:26:52.435 --> 00:26:55.187
In real life most sessions never produce siblings.

409
00:26:56.537 --> 00:26:59.609
